# Melony UI and SDUI Guidelines

The `@melony/ui-kit` and `@melony/ui-shadcn` packages provide the contract and components for Server-Driven UI (SDUI) in Melony.

## Base Contract (@melony/ui-kit)

`@melony/ui-kit` defines the standard contract for UI nodes and provides the `MelonyRenderer` component for recursive rendering.

### SDUI Conventions

- Use the `ui` helper (from `@melony/ui-kit`) on the server to create type-safe UI nodes.
- Prefer `card`, `row`, `col`, `text`, and `button` for standard layouts.
- Use `MelonyRenderer` for recursive rendering of UI nodes.

### Example Node Structure
```json
{
  "type": "card",
  "props": { "title": "Result" },
  "children": [{ "type": "text", "props": { "content": "Done!" } }]
}
```

## UI Kit (@melony/ui-shadcn)

`@melony/ui-shadcn` provides pre-built UI components using Shadcn/Base UI that satisfy the `@melony/ui-kit` contract.

### Setup

Register the components in your `MelonyUIProvider`.

```tsx
import { MelonyUIProvider } from "@melony/ui-kit";
import { shadcnElements } from "@melony/ui-shadcn";

export default function App({ children }) {
  return (
    <MelonyUIProvider components={shadcnElements}>
      {children}
    </MelonyUIProvider>
  );
}
```

## Best Practices

- Prefer composition of existing components over creating new ones when possible.
- Ensure all custom components follow the UI kit node contract.
- Use standard layout types (`row`, `col`) to ensure responsiveness.
